{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790459005,"nonce":"YqQKkgDz1QxfRz5WxgmF+Sq9nhA=","title":"AOT: a caribou native of a typed member calls its link symbol directly","message":"A Haxe program on caribou declares every foreign member as a native of the\n`caribou` library, `@:hlNative(\"caribou\", \"game:hud.Hud.add(_)\")`. Hosted,\ncaribou-ash registers each as a HostNative with a context word (the slot's\naddress) and `record: true`, and the JIT and interpreter pass the context.\nAOT cannot: llvm/function/natives.rs refuses a native with a context word\n(\"cannot be linked ahead of time\"). In a build where the natives are not\nregistered, each becomes a slot that hlp_aot_native fills at start from a\nlibrary `caribou` that doesn't exist, so the call raises when reached. So\nan AOT program reaches no plugin and no other language.\n\nDecided with the user (2026-09-26): link statically. A member with a typed\nsignature has a fixed C signature and a symbol named by caribou's rule\n(caribou crates/caribou/src/link.rs: `symbol`, `link`, `plan`;\ndocs/architecture/linking.md). For a `caribou` native whose signature\ntypes, the AOT emits a direct call to that symbol, declared external with\nthe rule's C signature, and the linker resolves it against the object that\ndefines it: a WrenLift Library object's thunk, a plugin's export, a Zyntax\nmodule's. The published set seeds reachability, so no body another\nlanguage calls is shaken out.\n\nUntyped members (`Dynamic`, a bare function type) do not link this way;\nthe build names them rather than emitting a call that raises (caribou\n0683393 has the report of which sites link and which stay dynamic).","files":null}]}